#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"1. Print at 100 % (“Actual size”), without “Fit to page”.\n"
"2. Measure the rulers (x: {x} mm, y: {y} mm) or the cutting frame\n"
"    ({frame}, between the dashed lines): the longest length is the most "
"accurate.\n"
"3. The dashed cutting frame must be printed entirely, on all four sides.\n"
"4. On each edge, note the smallest line printed entirely (2 to 6 mm from "
"the edge):\n"
"    this is the non-printable area on that side. Set print_margin_mm to "
"at least the\n"
"    largest of the four values, and below the assembly margin.\n"
"5. Scale error measured on a page WITHOUT correction: enter the expected "
"and measured\n"
"    lengths in the [printer] section of the preferences (File > "
"Preferences)."
msgstr ""

